00:43:50.128 --> 00:43:52.881
- Yeah. okay.
- Be careful. Let's get you on the boat.

724
00:43:54.299 --> 00:43:55.484
Okay.

725
00:43:55.508 --> 00:43:57.111
Is she the one
that makes out with all my friends?

726
00:43:57.135 --> 00:43:58.511
Yeah. Yeah. that's her.

727
00:43:59.596 --> 00:44:01.699
- Have I made out with her?
- Not yet.

728
00:44:01.723 --> 00:44:03.516
Let's get you inside.

729
00:44:22.035 --> 00:44:24.472
Thank you for walking me home.

730
00:44:24.496 --> 00:44:25.580
Yeah. Of course.

731
00:44:30.502 --> 00:44:35.215
Wait. so if I need something.
and I don't have service.

732
00:44:35.757 --> 00:44:38.342
- what do I...
- Just yell into the abyss.

733
00:44:39.677 --> 00:44:40.677
Sick. Okay.

734
00:44:41.429 --> 00:44:43.014
You're safe. though. I promise.

735
00:44:46.768 --> 00:44:48.728
Yeah. this is Canada. right?

736
00:44:49.938 --> 00:44:51.415
Nothing bad happens in Canada.

737
00:44:51.439 --> 00:44:54.734
Actually. no.
Bad shit happens. like. all the time.

738
00:44:55.819 --> 00:44:57.570
Just not on this island. though.

739
00:44:58.822 --> 00:45:00.323
Okay.

740
00:45:02.158 --> 00:45:03.618
- Bye.
- Bye.

741
00:45:23.763 --> 00:45:25.557
- Hello?
- Jesus!

742
00:45:30.728 --> 00:45:31.728
Who are you?

743
00:45:33.314 --> 00:45:34.314
Who are you?

744
00:45:36.443 --> 00:45:39.195
And what are you doing
in my grandfather's cottage?

745
00:45:51.249 --> 00:45:53.376
Connor. I have some very intense news.

746
00:45:53.585 --> 00:45:56.647
<i>Our mom. I think that she had
a secret biological daughter.</i>

747
00:45:56.671 --> 00:45:58.882
- Fuck!
- You said you'd be gone by the morning.

748
00:46:01.593 --> 00:46:03.386
<i>You said you were adopted?</i>

749
00:46:04.095 --> 00:46:05.930
- Yeah.
- So we're not related.

750
00:46:07.182 --> 00:46:09.118
- She hates me.
- Hey!

751
00:46:09.142 --> 00:46:11.686
She doesn't. Ramona
is... She's complicated.

752
00:46:15.356 --> 00:46:18.461
Being here. it's like.
"I don't have a mom."

753
00:46:18.485 --> 00:46:21.630
I feel like I want
to punch a wall or something!

754
00:46:21.654 --> 00:46:25.176
Yeah. that's something we call rage.
It's better to make friends with it.

755
00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:27.535
It's only gonna get worse as you age. so...

756
00:46:30.163 --> 00:46:32.516
I just feel like
everything I knew about myself was wrong.

757
00:46:32.540 --> 00:46:33.875
<i>That's a scary feeling.</i>

758
00:46:37.003 --> 00:46:39.255
It's good to be messy sometimes.
It's important.

759
00:46:40.882 --> 00:46:43.134
What do you know about my summer?
My summer.

760
00:46:43.760 --> 00:46:46.262
Well done. You just pushed me away
as far as you could.

761
00:46:47.096 --> 00:46:51.100
Your mom was the most fearless person
I've ever known.

762
00:46:54.103 --> 00:46:55.664
<i>Growing up and changing</i>

763
00:46:55.688 --> 00:46:58.733
and feeling out of control.
it's really freaky.

764
00:46:59.567 --> 00:47:01.361
<i>But it's also pretty exciting.</i>

765
00:47:03.154 --> 00:47:05.007
Do you feel like you got
the answers you wanted?

766
00:47:05.031 --> 00:47:07.283
I feel like I've barely
scratched the surface.

767
00:47:10.286 --> 00:47:13.122
You said. "No more secrets."
